Hi Avery,

Figma Make, which turns a prompt or an existing design into a working prototype with real code, is now available on every plan, including Starter.

What's new:
- Start from a Figma design and get a clickable, editable prototype
- Connect to sample data or your own API to test real flows
- Publish to a shareable link, or export the code

Also this month: Dev Mode now shows component usage across your codebase, and the Figma MCP server lets coding agents read your design files directly.

Try Figma Make: https://figma.com/make?ref=ga-0313

